<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 12 January, from 1528 to 2010.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/denmark" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1528 CE <span class="tih-ago">498 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gustav Vasa crowned King of Sweden at Uppsala</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Five years after his election ended the Kalmar Union with Denmark, Gustav I was crowned in Uppsala Cathedral. He went on to build a strong hereditary monarchy and introduce the Lutheran Reformation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1755 CE <span class="tih-ago">271 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Empress Elizabeth founds Moscow University</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Empress Elizabeth signed the decree founding Moscow University, proposed by Ivan Shuvalov and Mikhail Lomonosov (12 January Old Style). Russia's oldest university now bears Lomonosov's name.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1866 CE <span class="tih-ago">160 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aeronautical Society of Great Britain founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The society, later the Royal Aeronautical Society, was founded in London to study flight decades before the first aeroplane. It is the oldest aeronautical society in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1908 CE <span class="tih-ago">118 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First long-distance radio message sent from the Eiffel Tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A transmitter on the Eiffel Tower sent a wireless message over a record distance. The tower's value for military radio helped secure its future after its original 20-year permit.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1932 CE <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hattie Caraway becomes the first woman elected to the US Senate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Appointed to succeed her late husband, Hattie Caraway of Arkansas won a special election to keep the seat. She went on to win two full terms and served until 1945.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Red Army launches the Vistula-Oder Offensive</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces burst out of their bridgeheads in Poland and advanced some 500 km in under three weeks. By early February they stood on the Oder, about 70 km from Berlin.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1970 CE <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Biafra announces its surrender, ending the Nigerian Civil War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Biafra's acting leader Philip Effiong announced the end of the secessionist state's resistance. Between half a million and two million people had died, many from famine caused by the blockade.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2010 CE <span class="tih-ago">16 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catastrophic earthquake strikes Haiti</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.0 earthquake hit near Port-au-Prince, destroying much of the capital. Estimates of the dead range from about 100,000 to over 300,000, and more than a million people were left homeless.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a></div></div></li></ol>
